# dotfiles-Gentoo/gentoo/package.license
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# INSTALLED by bootstrap.sh to:
#
#     /etc/portage/package.license/90-dotfiles-Gentoo
#
# Skip with `./bootstrap.sh --no-portage-config`; remove by deleting that file.
#
# Portage's default ACCEPT_LICENSE is `-* @FREE`, so a package under a
# proprietary licence is masked no matter what its keywords say. Exactly one atom
# in this stack is affected — and without this line it fails with a licence mask
# rather than a keyword mask, which is a different error message for the same
# outcome: a permanent ✗ next to `op` in `core doctor`.
#
# This is a REAL choice, not a formality: accepting it means agreeing to
# 1Password's EULA. If you would rather not, delete the line and drop
# app-misc/1password-cli from the guru_install list in bootstrap.sh — Core's
# 1Password helpers (zsh/50-op.zsh) are all HAVE_OP-gated and simply stay quiet.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1Password CLI — proprietary; `op` in the doctor's data/net group.
app-misc/1password-cli *
